        "reference-legal-dong-code-change-to-gold-real-transaction-region-stats",
        "gold-real-transaction-region-stats-to-gold-parcel-real-transaction"
      ],
      "enabled": true,
      "enabled_since": "2026-11-10T18:00:00Z",
      "expected_outcome": {
        "changes_within_hours": null,
        "no_change_bound_reason": "Changes only when its inputs moved. That it is not behind them is the asset reconciler's lag (root ADR-0333) and its lane's behind-inputs bound (root ADR-0444); a change bound here would report a source that published nothing."
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "by_pnu_parcel_real_transaction_bake",
      "scope": "changed-keys",
      "interruptible": true,
      "commits": "as_it_goes",
      "description": "Reflect each new Gold snapshot of gold.parcel_real_transaction (the own-producer 실거래 kind, root ADR-0371) in R2 by-PNU serving (scripts/ops/by-pnu-serving-bake.sh parcel-real-transaction), as section packs (root ADR-0147, ADR-0193 §9): a change set decides a create-only patch, a reflect-only manifest or a full new generation, exactly as the panel bake does per lane. Its own job, as every own-producer kind's (root ADR-0303 §2): a slow national parcel re-bake in by_pnu_serving_bake never holds it. Nothing to do until the operator's first pack-only publish of the lane (root ADR-0190). Started when gold_parcel_real_transaction_rebuild commits a new snapshot, and at 10:50 as the fallback (root ADR-0171); each run's containers are its own one-offs (scripts/guard/batch-containers-are-run-scoped.sh). Two slots and MemoryMax=5G, the public-auction bake's bound: a scheduled run patches the parcels of the 법정동s a day's deals changed, and the lane's whole generation is the operator's cut-over bake (root ADR-0190), not this job's. Two slots, as the ownership bake, so it never runs beside both the panel bake and another 5G bake (root ADR-0138).",
      "capabilities": [
        "by_pnu_kind_section_pack_patches"
      ],
      "systemd_service": "foundation-by-pnu-lane-bake@parcel-real-transaction.service",
      "systemd_timer": null,
      "state_paths": [
        "/data/foundation-platform/by-pnu-bake"
      ],
      "schedule": "50 10 * * *",
      "started_by": "inputs",
      "stop_grace_minutes": 30,
      "wait_limit_minutes": 0,
      "time_limit_minutes": 115,
      "per_run_cap": {
        "unit": "run",
        "limits": [],
        "deadline": null,
        "measured_run_seconds": null,
        "first_run": {
          "estimate_seconds": 1500,
          "estimated_from": "computed from the parcel-ownership bake, the same by-pnu-serving-bake.sh: 636 s for 39,396,906 documents (2026-11-05, its cut-over's bake step); the lane bakes at most one document per served parcel (39,861,511), so 1,500 s, more than twice it; before the lane's first publish, which waits for whole history (root ADR-0350 §6), a run is `nothing to do: not cut over yet`"
        }
      },
      "pool": "spark",
      "pool_slots": 2,
      "priority_weight": 1,
      "priority_class": "publish",
      "retries": 0,
      "pipeline_graph_edges": [
        "gold-parcel-real-transaction-to-parcel-real-transaction-by-pnu-section-packs"
      ],
      "enabled": true,
      "enabled_since": "2026-11-10T18:00:00Z",
      "expected_outcome": {
        "changes_within_hours": null,
        "no_change_bound_reason": "Changes only when its inputs moved. That it is not behind them is the asset reconciler's lag (root ADR-0333) and its lane's behind-inputs bound (root ADR-0444); a change bound here would report a source that published nothing."
      }
    }
